{"id": "tea:bhiksuka-upanisad:1-bahudaka", "source": "src:bhiksuka-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (bahūdaka)"}, "paraphrase": "The bahūdakas carry triple staff and water-pot, keep topknot and thread, wear ochre and take eight mouthfuls from the houses of brahmin sages, avoiding honey and meat.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-kinds-of-renunciant"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhiksuka-upanisad:1-hamsa", "source": "src:bhiksuka-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (haṃsa)"}, "paraphrase": "The haṃsas stay one night in a village, five in a town, seven at a sacred place; they take cow's urine and dung and practise the lunar fast (cāndrāyaṇa).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-kinds-of-renunciant"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhiksuka-upanisad:1-kuticaka", "source": "src:bhiksuka-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (kuṭīcaka)"}, "paraphrase": "Among mendicants seeking liberation there are four kinds. The kuṭīcakas — such as Gautama, Bharadvāja, Yājñavalkya and Vasiṣṭha — live on eight mouthfuls and seek liberation by the path of yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-kinds-of-renunciant"], "teachers": ["tch:yajnavalkya", "tch:bharadvaja"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhiksuka-upanisad:1-paramahamsa", "source": "src:bhiksuka-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (paramahaṃsa)"}, "paraphrase": "The paramahaṃsas — Saṃvartaka, Āruṇi, Śvetaketu, Jaḍabharata, Dattātreya, Śuka, Vāmadeva, Hārītaka — take eight mouthfuls, live at tree-roots, empty houses and cremation grounds, clothed or naked; for them there is no dharma or adharma, pure or impure; they beg from all castes.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-kinds-of-renunciant", "cpt:ativarnasrami"], "teachers": ["tch:samvartaka", "tch:uddalaka-aruni", "tch:svetaketu", "tch:jadabharata", "tch:dattatreya", "tch:suka", "tch:vamadeva", "tch:haritaka"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
